Issue 2: MQTT motion sensor not updating
The predicates show 
cargo_checked
 — meaning either no motion was detected, or the MQTT message never arrived. Let's debug what Z-Wave is actually publishing:

Run
# Subscribe to see all Z-Wave MQTT messages in real time
mosquitto_sub -t "zwave/#" -v
Then move in front of the PIR sensor. You should see something like:

Run
zwave/Motion_sensor_status {"value":true,"time":1750001234567}
If you see nothing, the Z-Wave sensor might have fallen off the network (battery? range?). If you see messages but the format differs (e.g., the value is nested differently), the 
update()
 method in 
mqtt.py
 might not be matching the topic correctly.

Also check if the MQTT topic format changed — 
mqtt.py
 expects "Air_temperature" in the topic and topic.endswith("/Humidity"). Let me see what topics are actually being published:

Run
mosquitto_sub -t "zwave/#" -v | head -20
What do you see?
